{"spilled":1793633236.2177591,"input":{"command":"cd \/Users\/toddbruss\/Documents\/GitHub\/StarPlayrX && cp \/tmp\/spx-shots\/StarPlayrX-Mac-screenshot.png docs\/screenshot-mac.png && cp \/tmp\/spx-shots\/StarPlayrX-Mac-tear-off.png docs\/screenshot-mac-torn-off.png && cp \/tmp\/spx-shots\/StarPlayrX-Mac-shade.png docs\/screenshot-mac-shade.png && for m in Bubbles Soft-Bubbles No-Bubbles; do cp ~\/Desktop\/StarPlayrX-shots\/StarPlayrX-Mac-shade-$m.png docs\/screenshot-mac-shade-$(echo $m | tr A-Z a-z).png; done && ls docs | grep screenshot\npython3 - <<'E'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"- **Lava-lamp color equalizer:** live bars driven by the app's own audio (Core Audio process tap + FFT), with drifting colors and a glow that pulses on the beat. Needs macOS 14.2 or later\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Lava-lamp color equalizer:** 60 fps bars worked out from the audio as it's decoded, before it plays, so they stay in step with the music and need no \"record system audio\" permission. Drifting colors, a glow that pulses on the beat, and a darker glow on light backgrounds\n- **Lava-lamp bubbles:** soft bubbles rise inside the bars, faster when the music is louder, swelling and shrinking like wax in a lava lamp. **Single-click the bars to switch modes:** Bubbles → Soft Bubbles → No Bubbles → back to Bubbles. A little speech bubble pops up where you clicked to name the mode, and your choice is remembered (Soft Bubbles is the default). Double-clicking the bars still rolls the window up\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33%\"><img src=\"docs\/screenshot-mac-shade-bubbles.png\" width=\"260\" alt=\"Rolled-up StarPlayrX with Bubbles in the equalizer bars\"><br><b>🫧 Bubbles<\/b><\/td>\n    <td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33%\"><img src=\"docs\/screenshot-mac-shade-soft-bubbles.png\" width=\"260\" alt=\"Rolled-up StarPlayrX with Soft Bubbles in the equalizer bars\"><br><b>☁️ Soft Bubbles<\/b><\/td>\n    <td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33%\"><img src=\"docs\/screenshot-mac-shade-no-bubbles.png\" width=\"260\" alt=\"Rolled-up StarPlayrX with no bubbles in the equalizer bars\"><br><b>▮ No Bubbles<\/b><\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n<\/table>\n\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"- **Now Playing matches what you hear:** on live channels the song shown follows the audio's own timestamp, like the SiriusXM web player, and changes when the song in the audio changes.\",\n    \"- **Now Playing matches what you hear:** on live channels the song shown is held back by how far the audio runs behind the live feed, so it changes when the song you hear changes. The channel list's song info refreshes 3 times a minute.\")\nrep(\"[StarPlayrX for Mac 1.1.7](https:\/\/github.com\/AgentiLoop\/StarPlayrX\/releases\/tag\/mac-1.1.7)\",\"[StarPlayrX for Mac 1.1.8](https:\/\/github.com\/AgentiLoop\/StarPlayrX\/releases\/tag\/mac-1.1.8)\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngit add README.md docs && git commit -qm \"README: Mac 1.1.8, new screenshots, lava-lamp bubbles and how to switch modes\" && git push -q origin mustang && git status -sb | head -1 && git log --oneline -1"},"tool":"user_shell"}